/* This is a list of cores that implement RISC-V.

   Before using #include to read this file, define a macro:

      RISCV_CORE(CORE_NAME, ARCH, MICRO_ARCH, MVENDORID, MARCHID, MIMPID)

   The CORE_NAME is the name of the core, represented as a string.
   The ARCH is the default arch of the core, represented as a string,
   can be NULL if no default arch.
   The MICRO_ARCH is the name of the core for which scheduling decisions
   will be made, represented as an identifier.
   The MVENDORID, MARCHID and MIMPID are what the core reports in the
   registers of those names, which is how -mcpu=native and -mtune=native
   recognise the core they are running on.  They are riscv_core_id_t
   values, so a reader that uses them has to include
   common/config/riscv/riscv-hwprobe.h first.  A value that has not been
   recorded is UNKNOWN_ID, and a core is only recognised when all three
   registers are recorded and all three agree, so an entry that leaves any
   of them UNKNOWN_ID is never detected.

   If the core has an alternate name(s), an alias(es) can be created to map
   an alternate name to the core's canonical name.  Before using #include
   to read this file, define a macro:

      RISCV_CORE_ALIAS(CANONICAL_NAME, ALIAS_NAME)

   CANONICAL_NAME is the normal name of the core, represented as a string.
   ALIAS_NAME is the alternate name for the core, represented as a string.  */

#ifndef UNKNOWN_ID
#define UNKNOWN_ID ((riscv_core_id_t) -1)
#endif
#ifndef RISCV_CORE
#define RISCV_CORE(CORE_NAME, ARCH, MICRO_ARCH, MVENDORID, MARCHID, MIMPID)
#endif
#ifndef RISCV_CORE_ALIAS
#define RISCV_CORE_ALIAS(CANONICAL_NAME, ALIAS_NAME)
#endif

